+\subsection{A genuine original frame obstruction}\label{sec:obstruction}
+The frame restriction is substantive. The following direct corollary uses the already audited reversible clock of Report 49~\cite{report49}; it does not depend on the conditional uniform-chart imports.
+
+\begin{proposition}[Non Presburger absolute untimed reachability]\label{prop:obstruction}
+There is a globally reversible conservative binary CA $F$, with $F$ and $F^{-1}$ of radius at most $91$, whose forward untimed set of complete outputs from the single fixed input $\{0,5,6,13\}$ is not Presburger-definable in its four sorted absolute occupied coordinates. Its stationary-singleton frame has a Presburger-definable untimed orbit from that input.
+\end{proposition}
+\begin{proof}
+Call the radius-at-most-$90$ clock in Report 49 $G$ (that report calls it $F$). For $D\ge13$, put $C_D=\{0,5,6,D\}$ and $L_D=2D-22$. The report's complete-orbit proposition gives
+\begin{equation}\label{eq:priorclock}
+ G^s(C_D)=
+ \begin{cases}
+ \{0,5+s,6+s,D\},&0\le s\le D-11,\\
+ \{0,2D-18-s,2D-14-s,D+1\},&D-10\le s\le2D-23,
+ \end{cases}
+\end{equation}
+and $G^{L_D}(C_D)=C_{D+1}$. The displayed coordinates are strictly increasing in each range and their minimum is always zero. An isolated singleton is fixed, since every literal rule endpoint requires at least two particles.
+
+Set $F=\tau_1\circ G$. Translation commutes with $G$, so $F^t=\tau_t\circ G^t$ and $F^{-1}=G^{-1}\circ\tau_{-1}$. Both maps have radius at most $91$, preserve particle number and are inverse on the full shift. The singleton drift of $F$ is $1$, so its stationary frame is precisely $G$.
+
+From $C_{13}$, cycle $k$ starts at $t_k=k^2+3k$ and has gap $D=13+k$. Let $\mathcal R_F\subseteq\Z^4$ be the complete forward untimed output set, in sorted coordinates. Its minimum coordinate at physical time $t$ is $t$. Intersect $\mathcal R_F$ with the affine slice
+\[
+ y_2-y_1=5,\qquad y_3-y_1=6.
+\]
+The right phase of \eqref{eq:priorclock} meets this slice exactly at $s=0$. The left phase has middle-pair separation four and cannot meet a slice requiring separation one. The full phase bounds and sorting exclude spectator substitutions, including at the smallest gap $D=13$. Thus the exact intersection is
+\begin{equation}\label{eq:obstructionslice}
+ \{(t_k,t_k+5,t_k+6,t_k+13+k):k\in\N\}.
+\end{equation}
+If $\mathcal R_F$ were Presburger, intersection with this slice and projection onto $y_1$ would make $\{k^2+3k:k\in\N\}$ Presburger. A unary Presburger subset of $\N$ is eventually periodic~\cite{ginsburg}. Here successive gaps $2k+4$ tend to infinity: an eventual period $P\ge1$ would put $t_k+P$ strictly between consecutive terms for sufficiently large $k$, a contradiction.
+
+By contrast the complete stationary-frame untimed orbit is explicitly
+\begin{align*}
+ \mathcal R_G={}&\{(0,p,p+1,D):D\ge13,\ 5\le p\le D-6\}\\
+ &\quad\cup\{(0,q,q+4,E):E\ge14,\ 5\le q\le E-9\}.
+\end{align*}
+These are precisely the two phase ranges with $D=13+k$, and their union is Presburger. This proves both claims.
+\end{proof}
+
+Report 49's inherited binary theorem also proves that complete original-frame timed evolution is Presburger for every fixed input of at most three particles. Projecting away time preserves Presburger definability. Thus four is the least particle count for failure of fixed-input original-frame untimed reachability in the binary conservative model, including its globally reversible subclass. This sharpness deduction uses that explicitly credited lower-bound theorem in addition to the clock orbit.
+
+The failure already holds for one fixed anchored input, so a uniform original-frame untimed relation cannot always be Presburger either: specializing its input coordinates would give $\mathcal R_F$. These statements concern forward time and absolute coordinates. Quotienting outputs by arbitrary translation removes this particular obstruction. The remaining classification question is which additional rules or drift conditions preserve original-frame untimed regularity.
 
